# Technical acceptance: affected-input reexamination

The only changed prior inputs are the nine current skill evidence envelopes. Their exact old bytes survive in previous/, and support the original AC04 checkpoint (8 technical approved, 3 inconclusive, 25 unverified). The original technical-acceptance/spec.md is unchanged: its migration experiment is historical; the new pending-criterion execution is explicitly scoped in skill-consumer-validation. No unconditional freeze is reinstated and no historical result is rewritten.

AC01/02: checker, validator, gate and eight adversarial fixture tests are unchanged. All five states and required content bindings still apply. New per-criterion records have actual consumer/oracle sources, execution artifacts and semantic reviews; decisions are scoped to bounded fixtures, not current product implementations.
AC03: independent portability remains a requirement. The final successor feature validates a fresh export without application sources, including these new portable consumers. The unchanged previous export receipt remains evidence of the prior experiment, not an assertion about a future export.
AC04: compare the exact old nine envelopes against before.json and inspect all 28 successor records/matrix. Previously accepted 26 requirement objects are unchanged; pending 3+25 now have new observations. All original 36 scenario definitions are byte-identical. This new review preserves the historical checkpoint and explicitly names its successor.

The completed original tests/exports are reused only for unchanged code. New governance executions are recorded by the successor feature; hashes are not silently refreshed around an old result.
